00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.030 align:start position:0%
 
does being a vc  make you a better entrepreneur so i got  a great question from one of my youtube  viewers  uh kevin love you guys and he wrote in  to say  would you say getting into a vc would  help you gain skills that would make you  a better business owner  and or angel investor so vc here is  venture capitalist  and i would respond to that absolutely  so when i  when i sold my software company i didn't  know what i was going to do next i wish  i could see i had this clear plan here's  my next steps here's where i'm going  i had no idea and i was i was  frustrated and scared i was kind of  looking for my next  passion project to jump into and i think  we all go through these periods in our  lives where we're not sure what we want  to do next right  and the way to get through that isn't to  force  ideas on yourself and force projects on  yourself but to explore  see what things are interesting for you  and just start to explore and see if  you'd like it or not so i tried a whole  bunch of stuff i tried  rock climbing i tried salsa dancing i  tried getting to venture capital firm  just to see you know not having  expectations just to see what i liked  the reason for getting into venture  capital was with my business  we never needed venture capital we came  close  uh we thought about it we had potential  opportunities but we never actually got  funding for a business our business got  acquired before we went for funding  so it was always one of those things  that i was kind of interested in to see  what it was like  and because i didn't have a business  idea for what to do next i thought  maybe i'll just learn about the vc world  and raising capital and see what it's  like and see if i enjoy it  it could have been something that i  tried for a week and hated it i was  fortunate enough to hook up with  a company in toronto where the main  partners were in their 60s or 70s they  had a whole ton of experience  and they needed help bringing in new  people new businesses  if they could get the businesses they  knew where to go for the funding  so my role is to come in and help them  find new businesses i had friends who  were growing their companies  who needed advice who needed expansion  capital so it seemed like a good fit  and along the way  i learned not just about how to raise  capital  which was great right you see  entrepreneurs come in and they're  getting  asked questions by the main partners at  my firm  and you know i didn't know the answers  to those questions so i had to think  about it too i thought  well for my next venture of irony  capital now i have it all figured out  and it was also great to see how these  businesses  presented themselves how they grew to  where they were  right so part of my job was screening  business plans  and like 99.5  of the plans that came in got rejected  and so i got this  to learn quickly what the difference was  between a great plan and all the others  so i knew if i was writing a business  plan how to make it great  when they came in and they they  presented i got to see how they  presented i got to see what their story  was i got to see who was on their team  how they built their companies  and all that was being soaked up  so i knew if i launched a new company i  could take all that knowledge with me  i got to see how companies grew so  quickly  and what made them so successful and i  gained great contacts through it as well  and again i could use all that i didn't  know  there was no great plan but i was just  learning i was enjoying the learning  process  i was there for maybe two years just  under two years  and through that process i started  working on my own  website and didn't know if it would be a  business or what would happen but it  just started to take off  and i felt like i had learned what i  needed to learn  from the venture capital business and  decided i'm going to leave that  i'm going to do my own thing off of  every carmichael.com in that group  you'll find with things in your life  that  some things you'll love for a little bit  some things you'll love for a long time  and that's okay  you know the vc world i loved for a  little bit and then my passion  fell i felt like i had learned what i  needed to learn and i wasn't excited by  it anymore  that's the time to leave and go do  something else where too many people  feel like oh well getting these skills  i'm really good at this so even though  i'm not that interested in it  i'm gonna keep going because it's a good  career path for me or i can make a lot  of money doing it  if you're not excited by it anymore you  have to move on and do something else  and entrepreneurship was really what was  exciting me and my website  and helping other business owners really  excited me and still does today it's i  still  love it today it's been 12 years i don't  know how long it's been i still love it  it's still great for me if i ever lose  my interest for helping entrepreneurs  then i'll go do something else  but you always have to follow your  passion that's what got me into the vc  world  it definitely made me a better  entrepreneur it definitely made me a  better  angel investor but again you know go  into it  if you're feeling like you love it and  you feel like you want to learn about it  and the moment that that passion stops  then go find something else and it's  okay not to know where you're gonna go  but you know that you're on the path and  if you continue searching you're going  to find something you love  and can hopefully build a massively  successful  and rewarding and fulfilling business  around believe  for those of you watching like the video  please give it a thumbs up below you  have a question or comment leave it  below and i can make a video response  for you  and click on my face to subscribe to the  channel thank you guys for watching so  much  and i'll see you soon

